{% comment %}
  IMPORTANT: WHEN USING THE SWIPERJS

  1. When a Swiper sits inside a flex container with flex-direction: row, its children can shrink or grow horizontally.
     Solution: You should give the Swiper container/wrapper a fixed size (using width, max-width, or flex: 0 0 <width>) to keep slide sizing stable.
              In a flex column or a normal block layout the element naturally fills the available width, so explicit width is usually not needed.

  2. When a swiper is inside a block container and that block container is inside a grid container.
    CSS Grid stretches its children by default, so even if the Swiper sits inside a block-level wrapper,
    the grid cell will stretch and allow the Swiper (and its images) to expand.
    Also, Swiper slides/images themselves can grow if their intrinsic size or Swiper settings allow it.

    Solution: You should give the Swiper container/wrapper a fixed size (using width or max-width) or add (grid-template-columns: repeat(1, minmax(0, 1fr))) on the grid container.

    NOTE: OR JUST ADD A (MIN-WIDTH: 0) OF THE PARENT ELEMENT THAT INSIDE OF THAT FLEX OR GRID ELEMENT.
    WHY THIS WORK: FLEX ITEMS HAVE A DEFAULT (MIN-WIDTH: AUTO), WHICH PREVENTS THEM FROM SHRINKING BELOW THEIR CONTENT SIZE. SETTING (MIN-WIDTH: 0) ALLOWS THE FLEX ITEM TO SHRINK PROPERLY.
{% endcomment %}

